{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user (cobbler orchestrator) assigned task #5307: \"[stitch] cmd/sha1sum -- srd031 R2.1-R2.3, R3.1\". The task requires implementing SHA-1 checksum verification features and binary/text mode flags for the sha1sum utility. Specifically:\n   - R2.1: --check FILE must parse GNU or BSD tag format checksums and recompute/compare digests\n   - R2.2: Print \"FILENAME: OK\" or \"FILENAME: FAILED\" for each entry; exit 1 if any check fails\n   - R2.3: --warn prints warnings for malformed lines; --quiet suppresses OK lines; --status suppresses all output\n   - R3.1: -b marks binary mode (HASH *FILENAME), -t is text mode default (HASH  FILENAME)\n   \n   Files to modify: cmd/sha1sum/main.go and cmd/sha1sum/sha1sum_test.go.\n   Acceptance criteria: go build compiles, go test passes, all R2.1-R2.3 and R3.1 requirements implemented.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - GNU sha1sum checksum format: \"HASH  FILENAME\" (text) or \"HASH *FILENAME\" (binary)\n   - BSD tag format: \"SHA1 (FILENAME) = HASH\"\n   - pkg/hashutil library: FormatGNU, FormatBSDTag, ParseChecksumLine, VerifyChecksums, DigestFiles, CheckOptions\n   - pkg/testutils differential testing: RunDiffTests comparing Go binary against gsha1sum reference\n   - SIGPIPE handling via pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler\n   - cobbler-scaffold pipeline: stitch tasks generate code from SRD specs\n   - Git is managed externally - NO git commands allowed\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - **docs/specs/software-requirements/srd031-sha1sum.yaml** (SRD specification)\n     - Defines R1 (digest computation), R2 (checksum verification), R3 (binary/text mode), R4 (exit codes/SIGPIPE)\n     - package_contract imports: pkg/hashutil, pkg/sys\n     - Non-goals: no HMAC-SHA1, SHA-1 is for GNU compatibility only\n\n   - **cmd/sha1sum/main.go** (existing implementation - 118 lines)\n     - ALREADY implements check mode (R2.1-R2.3) via hashutil.VerifyChecksums with CheckOptions{Warn, Quiet, Status}\n     - ALREADY implements binary/text mode flags (R3.1)\n     - Has complete flag parsing for --binary/-b, --text/-t, --tag, --check/-c, --warn/-w, --quiet, --status\n     - Full code:\n     ```go\n     // Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.\n     // SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n     package main\n     import (\n         \"crypto/sha1\"\n         \"fmt\"\n         \"os\"\n         \"strings\"\n         \"github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/hashutil\"\n         \"github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys\"\n     )\n     func main() {\n         sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()\n         opts, files := parseArgs(os.Args[1:])\n         cfg := hashutil.HashConfig{Algorithm: \"SHA1\", NewHash: sha1.New, DigestLen: 20}\n         if opts.check {\n             checkOpts := hashutil.CheckOptions{Warn: opts.warn, Quiet: opts.quiet, Status: opts.status}\n             exitCode := 0\n             for _, f := range files {\n                 ok, err := hashutil.VerifyChecksums(f, cfg, checkOpts, os.Stdout, os.Stderr)\n                 if err != nil {\n                     fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"sha1sum: %s\\n\", err)\n                     exitCode = 1\n                 } else if !ok {\n                     exitCode = 1\n                 }\n             }\n             os.Exit(exitCode)\n         }\n         os.Exit(hashutil.DigestFiles(files, cfg, opts.binary, opts.tag, os.Stdout, os.Stderr))\n     }\n     // options struct and parseArgs, parseLongFlag, parseShortFlags functions handle all flags\n     ```\n\n   - **cmd/sha1sum/sha1sum_test.go** (existing tests - 316 lines)\n     - ALREADY has comprehensive differential tests for R2.1-R2.3 and R3.1\n     - Tests include: check-valid, check-multi-valid, check-mismatch, check-mixed, check-bsd-tag, check-warn-malformed, check-quiet-all-ok, check-quiet-with-fail, check-status-ok, check-status-fail, check-short-flag, binary-multiple-files, binary-stdin, binary-long-flag, text-multiple-files, tag-binary-multiple\n     - Uses testutils.RunDiffTests against gsha1sum reference binary\n     - Has TestSIGPIPE test\n     - Helper functions: sha1hex, writeFile\n\n   - **pkg/hashutil contracts** (from package_contracts in prompt):\n     - HashConfig: {Algorithm string, NewHash func() hash.Hash, DigestLen int}\n     - CheckOptions: {Warn bool, Quiet bool, Status bool}\n     - FormatGNU(digest, filename string, binary bool) string\n     - FormatBSDTag(algorithm, filename, digest string) string\n     - VerifyChecksums(checksumFile string, cfg HashConfig, opts CheckOptions, stdout, stderr io.Writer) (bool, error)\n     - DigestFiles(files []string, cfg HashConfig, binary, tag bool, stdout, stderr io.Writer) int\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors encountered yet. The conversation was interrupted after the initial file reads.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - After reading the three required files, I discovered that the existing implementation in main.go and sha1sum_test.go ALREADY appears to contain complete implementations and tests for R2.1-R2.3 and R3.1 (likely carried over from the R1.1-R1.4 task #5306 which preceded this one).\n   - The critical question for continuing: Does the existing code fully satisfy all requirements, or are there gaps? The code appears complete but needs verification via `go build` and `go test`.\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - The initial message is the full stitch task description with extensive project context, SRDs, architecture, constitutions, package contracts, and task requirements for implementing srd031 R2.1-R2.3 and R3.1.\n   - \"CRITICAL: Respond with TEXT ONLY. Do NOT call any tools.\" - requesting this summary.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Verify that the existing code already satisfies R2.1-R2.3 and R3.1 (it appears to)\n